{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<h1>Mutations</h1>
<p class="hint">An address that accepts a <strong>POST</strong> and runs a program. A page renders
  and never writes; this is where writing lives &mdash; a different address, a different method, and
  a signed-in member with a valid form token. That split is what makes it safe to say a crawler
  cannot change anything by reading the site.</p>

<div class="doing"><a class="btn" href="{{newUrl}}">New mutation</a></div>

{{^any}}<p class="hint">None yet.</p>{{/any}}
{{#any}}
<p class="count">{{count}}</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>address</th><th>state</th><th>updated</th><th></th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{#mutations}}<tr>
    <td class="mono"><a href="{{editUrl}}">{{uri}}</a></td>
    <td>{{#enabled}}<span class="pill good">answering</span>{{/enabled}}{{^enabled}}<span class="pill dim">off</span>{{/enabled}}</td>
    <td class="dim mono">{{updated}}</td>
    <td class="actions"><a href="{{editUrl}}">edit</a></td>
  </tr>{{/mutations}}</tbody>
</table>
{{/any}}
<p class="hint">Tables are declared under <a href="{{tablesUrl}}">Tables</a>; each one a mutation can
  change gives it a <code>_merge_by_id</code> function.</p>
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
